<Base title="Privacy, submissions and browser-local plans"><article class="container"><div class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">YOUR INFORMATION</span><h1>A local plan.<br/>A private conversation.</h1><p class="lede">Planning inputs stay in your browser. Information you intentionally submit through an ELN form is stored separately for the owner to review and respond.</p></div><div class="article-body" style="max-width:800px"><h2>Your expansion plan</h2><p>The planning tools calculate in your browser. Remembering a draft on this device is optional and off by default. If enabled, local storage retains your working plan in that browser profile. Someone using the same profile may be able to access it.</p><p>Use the reset control in the planning workspace to remove the saved draft, or clear this site’s storage in your browser settings. JSON and printable brief exports are created locally. Clearing site data can permanently remove an unexported draft. Plan inputs are not automatically attached to either form or sent to the owner.</p><h2>Interest and contact forms</h2><p>The <a href="/interest/">interest form</a> asks for name, company, annual recurring revenue (ARR) and email. ARR is optional; you can state the currency and amount, “not recurring” or “not known.” The <a href="/contact/">contact form</a> asks for your comments and email. Use it for enquiries, corrections and privacy requests.</p><p>ELN uses those details to review and respond to the request you submitted. Submissions are visible in an owner-only board protected by sign-in. The forms do not subscribe you to a mailing list or publish your details. Please keep confidential contracts, payment credentials and sensitive personal records out of comments.</p><h2>Retention and your controls</h2><p>The application automatically removes form submissions after 365 days from submission. The owner can delete a record earlier. To request access, correction or deletion, use the contact form and identify the email you used; verification may be needed before a record is disclosed or changed.</p><p>Deleting a live record does not remove copies already exported by the owner, correspondence held elsewhere, or provider records subject to separate retention. No application backup schedule or external form-processing service is configured in this release. The owner should manage any exported copies consistently with the original purpose and your request.</p><h2>Storage and access</h2><p>Submitted form information is held in a database on persistent Railway storage. It is separate from public guides and browser-local plans. Public API requests cannot read the owner’s board, exports or records. Passwords are stored as salted hashes, and sign-in sessions use an HTTP-only cookie that expires after 12 hours.</p><p>The application does not log submitted names, email addresses, comments, ARR values or passwords. Short-lived, keyed hashes are used in memory to limit abuse; raw IP addresses are not stored by this application for that purpose. The hosting provider processes ordinary network requests separately.</p><h2>Cookies and tracking</h2><p>The public forms do not require an account cookie. The owner board sets a necessary sign-in cookie for its owner. The optional planning draft uses browser local storage. This build has no advertising pixel, third-party analytics service, embedded chat widget or automatic marketing emails. Fonts and application assets are served with the site.</p><h2>Hosting requests and provider terms</h2><p>The application runs in Railway’s U.S. West region. The provider can process IP addresses, request paths, browser information and timestamps to deliver and protect the service. The application sends form values in request bodies, not public URLs.</p><p>Railway’s published <a href="https://docs.railway.com/observability/logs">log documentation</a> gives the current Hobby plan seven days of displayed log history and says a plan upgrade can restore older logs. This is not a guarantee that every provider record is permanently erased after seven days. No third-party log forwarding is configured here.</p><p>Railway publishes a <a href="https://railway.com/legal/dpa">Data Processing Addendum</a> with separate roles for customer data and its own account/usage data. Publication of that document does not establish execution for this account. Applicable processing, transfer and retention arrangements remain the operator’s responsibility.</p><h2>Contact ELN</h2><p>Send questions or a data request through <a href="/contact/">Contact us</a>. Include the relevant page or the email used for your submission. Your contact details are used for a private response.</p><p class="meta">Updated 12 November 2026 for the ELN forms and owner board. Provider documents received AI-assisted source review; no professional privacy review is claimed.</p></div></article></Base>
